macOS 15.8.1, 2026-11-01, swiftc -O, one process per line.

plain 100:    alive; fitting (34.0, 16.0); leaf body ran
plain 500:    alive; fitting (34.0, 16.0); leaf body ran
plain 1000:   alive; fitting (34.0, 16.0); leaf body ran
plain 2000:   SIGSEGV
plain 5000:   SIGSEGV
plain 20000:  SIGSEGV
any 100:      alive; fitting (34.0, 16.0); leaf body ran
any 500:      alive; fitting (34.0, 16.0); leaf body ran
any 2000:     SIGSEGV
any 5000:     SIGSEGV
forever:      SIGSEGV

SwiftUI has no depth limit of its own to copy: past about the depth TUI's stack
guard stops at, the process dies. TUI does not follow it there (owner's rule:
never crash).
